r3-mini: snand env — USB-presence branch + verify-before-write (NAND & eMMC)

Provisioning u-boot picks its job by USB presence (not by golden presence — a
serial boot may be to *rewrite* the golden), and validates BEFORE erasing/writing:

  bootcmd: USB stick with snand-factory.bin present -> flash_nand (USB->NAND);
           else -> emmc_install (NAND->eMMC).

  flash_nand: crc32 the loaded image and cmp.b against the `snand-factory.crc`
    sidecar (BE 4-byte CRC32, generated by make-flashkit) -> ONLY on match does it
    `mtd erase`+`mtd write`; then read-back + cmp.b verifies the write. A bad/corrupt
    USB image fails the CRC and the NAND is never touched.

  emmc_install: `ubi read fit && iminfo` validates the slot image BEFORE any eMMC
    write; the NAND source itself was CRC-verified when it was flashed. Reuses
    golden_restore's gr_bl/gr_slots (bl2/fip/gpt + both slots) + mmc rescan; solid
    green LED on success for no-serial operators (this board's blue LEDs sit on
    strap pins and are not drivable from u-boot, so we use the one usable LED).

USB plugged = (re)flash NAND incl. its own BL2+u-boot (full snand-factory.bin);
USB removed = provision eMMC. Hardware-validated 2026-06-13 (CRC verify-before-
write, read-back, eMMC both slots).
